<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	The launch screen is the splash's own field with no orb in it yet: the first frame the app
	draws puts the orb on that same color, so the handoff is a field that does not change. An
	image here could not do that. A launch screen holds one image at its natural size, so the
	orb would be drawn at a different scale on every screen and would jump when the responsive
	splash replaced it.

	This dictionary is the reason the target carries a real Info.plist: a nested dictionary has
	no INFOPLIST_KEY_ setting. Every flat key the app needs is still a build setting.
	-->
	<key>UILaunchScreen</key>
	<dict>
		<key>UIColorName</key>
		<string>LaunchField</string>
	</dict>
	<!--
	Playback continues with the screen locked. An array is the second thing no INFOPLIST_KEY_
	setting can express, so this key lived in project.yml as a setting that never reached a
	built product. macOS ignores it.
	-->
	<key>UIBackgroundModes</key>
	<array>
		<string>audio</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
